/// Files included in the program when it is built, so a single executable
/// ships its templates, migrations, and static assets. Call `Embed.text` or
/// `Embed.bytes` in a module constant: `const page = Embed.text("index.html")`.
///
/// The path is a text literal relative to the directory of the module that
/// calls it, with `/` between segments, and stays inside that directory: no
/// absolute path and no empty, `.`, or `..` segment. The build reads the file,
/// so the executable needs no file at run time. A call outside a constant's
/// initializer, or inside a function value in one, is `E5206`; a path that is
/// not such a literal is `E5207`; a file the build cannot read is `E5208`.

import std/bytes.{Bytes}

// 7. Conversions.

/// Returns the contents of the file at `path`, which must be UTF-8 (`E5209`
/// otherwise).
///
/// Cost: none at run time; the constant holds the text.
pub native fn text(path: Text) -> Text

/// Returns the contents of the file at `path`.
///
/// Cost: none at run time; the constant holds the bytes.
pub native fn bytes(path: Text) -> Bytes
